#!/bin/bash
# 723 (Fri 27 Nov 2026 08:32-08:35, Peter: "why can't you think about it in a less formulaic way" and "with racing why you
# haven't carved out each type of race, it seems a narrow view"). Adds two instructions to the sport briefs before the racing,
# golf and cricket sessions start (they read the brief when they start; tennis is already running and gets a note file).
# Paper and trial only. No orders. Nothing deleted.
B=/root/pe-builder
cat >> $B/BRIEF_sport_racing.md <<'EOF'

ADDED 27 Nov 08:40 ON PETER'S ORDER - RACING IS NOT ONE SPORT. So far racing was measured as one lump and that is why nothing showed. Carve it and run every step above separately for EACH type, then the types against each other: flat turf / all-weather / hurdles / chases / bumpers (national hunt flat); handicap / non-handicap; maiden, novice, seller, claimer, nursery, conditions, listed and group or graded; class 1 to 7; age band (two-year-olds, three-year-olds, older); distance band (sprint 5-6f, 7f-1m, middle, staying; jumps 2m, 2m4f, 3m+); field size (2-4, 5-7, 8-11, 12-15, 16+, because place terms change at 5, 8 and 16); going; course and course-by-distance (draw only matters on some); time of day and day of week (evening and midweek cards are thinner); Britain against Ireland; first race against last race of a card. For each type say: how right is the price before the off, how much money is in the market, who is in it (big festival money or a handful of people), how it behaves in running (front-runners in sprints, fallers in chases, long-distance races where the price moves slowly enough for a five-second trade), and where the place and other markets disagree with the win market. A type with under 30 races is reported as too few, not as a no. Show the table of types in the report, best first, with the count beside each.
EOF
lens='
ADDED 27 Nov 08:40 ON PETER'"'"'S ORDER - THINK LIKE A SMALL TRADER, NOT A TEXTBOOK. Peter needs a small amount each month, not millions, and that is our one real advantage: we can work where the professionals cannot be bothered because the money is too small for them. Our only winner so far (T1) is exactly that: a football market with under £5,000 in it. So in this sport look FIRST where the money is thin and the crowd is casual, and ask of every market: who is on the other side, and are they forced or careless? Specifically: (a) every result by money matched in the market (under £1k, £1-5k, £5-20k, £20k+) - is the price less right where there is less money; (b) the side markets nobody watches against the main market of the same event at the same second - when the main market has moved and the side market has not, that is a price left behind by someone who is not looking, and we can take it; (c) the minor events, lower tiers, overseas and women'"'"'s events, early rounds, the first and last hour of trading; (d) moments when people MUST trade whatever the price: closing a position just before the start or at a break, a favourite'"'"'s backers cashing out after a setback, the rush in the last seconds; (e) prices left on offer after the news has changed (a non-runner, a withdrawal, a wicket, a break of serve, the weather) - how long do stale offers sit, and for how much. Measure how many £ a day is there at stakes of £2 to £50, which is all we need. Put what you find under its own heading, Small markets, in the report.'
for s in racing golf cricket; do printf '%s\n' "$lens" >> $B/BRIEF_sport_$s.md; done
mkdir -p /root/pe-sports/sports/tennis; printf '%s\n' "$lens" > /root/pe-sports/sports/tennis/ADDED_27NOV.md
# football gets the same small-market lens as its own session, queued behind lane 2 (two heavy sessions at a time)
cat > $B/BRIEF_small_football.md <<EOF
You are a Builder on Peter Edwards' trading server: the football small-markets session, 27 Nov 2026. Read /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_league.md first; all of it applies with STANDING RULE 708. Paper and trial only; never an order endpoint; nothing deleted; credentials only through /root/pe-queue/runner/creds.py; exchanges only; no lay at 5.0 or longer. Memory: never more than about 5 GB yourself, one day of ticks at a time. Work in /root/pe-sports/sports/football_small; do not edit grid, the paper trader, trial.py or the goal signal; add trial rules the documented way and say what you added.
WHAT WE KNOW: the only rule in profit is T1 (back the favourite in match-result markets with under £5,000 matched, two minutes before the start: +25.6 per £100 on 283 markets, six days all in profit). Nobody has asked WHY it works or what else is like it. Do that: (1) why - which leagues, which price bands, what time of day, how the price moved in the last hour, is the favourite simply under-backed where there is no crowd; does it hold at the price actually on offer for £10, £25 and £50, not only £2; (2) the same question for every other football market type we record (all 61 types now) by money matched; (3) side markets left behind by the main market in the same match at the same second, before the start and in play after a goal or a red card - how long the stale price sits and for how much money.
$lens
REPORT /root/pe-queue/reports/small_markets_football.md, plain English, one screen: line 1 why T1 works and whether it survives bigger stakes; line 2 how many more like it and the £ a day at £40; line 3 what went on trial; then the survivors as sentences. Commit and push: cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/small_markets_football.md && git commit -qm "football small markets: why T1 works and what else is like it" && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q. Then end the session.
EOF
cat > $B/run_small_football.sh <<'SH'
#!/bin/bash
CL=$(cat /root/pe-watchman/claude_path); ts=$(date -u +%F_%H%M); mkdir -p /root/pe-sports/sports/football_small
cd /root/pe-sports/sports/football_small && timeout -k 60 21600 "$CL" -p "$(cat /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_small_football.md)" --allowedTools "Bash,Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep" --max-turns 500 --output-format text > /root/pe-builder/runs/${ts}_small_football.log 2>&1
echo "small football session ended $(date -u '+%F %H:%M') exit $?" >> /root/pe-builder/sessions.log
SH
chmod +x $B/run_small_football.sh
grep -q run_small_football $B/run_lane2_722.sh || echo "/root/pe-builder/run_small_football.sh" >> $B/run_lane2_722.sh
rs=$(pgrep -fc '[r]un_sport_racing.sh'); rd=$(pgrep -fc '[r]un_ready.sh')
echo "723 done $(date -u +%H:%M) UTC: racing brief now carves every race type ($(grep -c 'RACING IS NOT ONE SPORT' $B/BRIEF_sport_racing.md)); small-market lens in racing/golf/cricket briefs ($(grep -lc 'SMALL TRADER' $B/BRIEF_sport_{racing,golf,cricket}.md | wc -l) of 3) and as a note for tennis; football small-markets session queued behind cricket. Racing session already started before this edit: $rs (0 = it will read the new brief). Readiness check running: $rd." >> /root/pe-queue/reports/running_now.md
cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/running_now.md && git commit -qm "running now: 723" -q && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q
